WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.880
Which number is larger when most of the
digits match?

2
00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.060
Compare from the greatest place value, not
from the right.

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.840
For whole numbers with no leading zeros,
more digits means

4
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.270
a larger number. If the lengths match,
compare one column

5
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.410
at a time. Compare four hundred and fifty
six thousand,

6
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.340
seven hundred and eighty two, with four
hundred and fifty

7
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.970
six thousand, seven hundred and twenty
eight.

8
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.550
Their hundred thousands, ten thousands,
thousands and hundreds match.

9
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.670
We have not found a difference yet, so
keep moving

10
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.490
right. At the tens place, eight is greater
than two.

11
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.860
Stop there. The first number is greater,
so four hundred

12
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.730
and fifty six thousand, seven hundred and
eighty two is

13
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.520
greater than four hundred and fifty six
thousand, seven hundred

14
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.050
and twenty eight. The ones cannot overturn
that difference.

15
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.660
Now compare three hundred and nine
thousand, nine hundred and

16
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.750
fifty, with three hundred and ten thousand
and five.

17
00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.340
The hundred thousands match.

18
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.410
At ten thousands, zero is less than one.

19
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.170
Therefore three hundred and nine thousand,
nine hundred and fifty

20
00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.210
is smaller. To order several numbers,
repeat the same method.

21
00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.180
Eighty nine thousand, nine hundred and
ninety nine comes before

22
00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.250
ninety thousand and one, which comes
before ninety thousand and

23
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.530
ten. Do not compare only the final three
digits.

24
00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.930
The greatest differing place decides.

25
00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.770
As a supporting estimation check, rounding
eighty nine thousand, nine

26
00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.250
hundred and ninety nine to the nearest
thousand gives ninety

27
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.430
thousand. A rounded value is useful, but
it does not

28
00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.990
replace an exact comparison.

29
00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:31.100
Recap: line up the places, start left,
find the first

30
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.010
difference, and explain your order.

